{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2105","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2105","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2105\",\"parent_revision\":\"f5fa1360a7610aaaf49a21a5c0585c4062b352e7\",\"root_revision\":\"8c07ecbe66bfc9ce2d9c83978c2ca426ac3ed13d7f682dbc6409f7219f409cf6\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **configurable gate composition for /complete-implementation per project** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/developer-tools/no-mistakes.md \u2014 pattern: Multi-Stage Composable Gates (Patterns Worth Adopting / Configuration section)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-05-03\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-05-04)\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\n**Status**: APPROVED-WITH-GAPS\\n\\n| Input | Status | Source |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Functional intent | PRESENT | Item description \u2014 clear target state with .dh/quality-gates.yaml and fallback behavior |\\n| Scope boundaries | PARTIAL | PQG path (build_proportional_quality_gate_plan, 3-task plan) not addressed |\\n| External interfaces | PRESENT | build_quality_gate_plan() in sam_schema/core/quality_gates.py verified; SKILL.md dispatch loop verified |\\n| Constraints | PARTIAL | No YAML schema validation approach stated; T5-skip interaction with reordering not addressed; type-safety of config reader not specified |\\n| Existing system context | PRESENT | _PHASE_DEFINITIONS list verified at quality_gates.py:24\u201373; build_quality_gate_plan() is a pure function (no I/O) |\\n| Verification expectations | PRESENT | Measurable signal is explicit and runnable |\\n\\nGaps (PARTIAL conditions):\\n- PQG path: item is silent on whether proportional gates (build_proportional_quality_gate_plan) are also made configurable\\n- T5 conditional skip: the dispatch loop in SKILL.md independently skips T5 when T4 finds no drift (lines 504\u2013506); how a reordered/renamed gate interacts with this hard-coded phase-name check is unspecified\\n- Config validation: no decision on whether invalid config (unknown gate name, duplicate IDs) should hard-error or fall back to defaults\\n- Type safety: the config reader will deserialize YAML into gate objects \u2014 no decision on TypedDict vs Pydantic model for the config schema\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\n1. Open any project that uses /complete-implementation.\\n2. Run /complete-implementation on a completed feature issue.\\n3. Observe that T1\u2013T6 execute unconditionally \u2014 no way to skip Feature Verification (T2) for a docs-only repo without modifying Python source.\\n4. Observe that the only skip mechanism is T5 (auto-skipped when T4 reports no drift), which is hardcoded in the SKILL.md dispatch logic, not in a config file.\\n\\n### Output / Evidence\\n\\n- Source of hardcoding: `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/quality_gates.py` lines 24\u201373 (`_PHASE_DEFINITIONS` list)\\n- Call site: `plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md` lines 408\u2013413 (`build_quality_gate_plan` call)\\n- Dispatch loop: `plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md` lines 442\u2013513 (6-phase SAM Dispatch Loop)\\n- Only existing conditional: SKILL.md lines 504\u2013506 (T5 skip when T4 reports no drift) \u2014 cannot be disabled or generalised via config\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n6/10 \u2014 Reduces friction for projects where not all 6 gates are applicable (e.g. docs-only repos, tooling-only repos without deployable services). Blocked by no critical path work. The T5 auto-skip is the only current flexibility; adding this config would generalise that pattern.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: nothing directly; this is an ergonomics improvement\\n- Bottleneck: every project using /complete-implementation runs the full 6-gate sequence even when 1\u20132 gates are irrelevant, wasting agent tokens and time\\n- Blast radius: changes touch `sam_schema/core/quality_gates.py` (pure function, easy to test), `complete-implementation/SKILL.md` (dispatch loop instructions), and a new schema reference file\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Project owners can disable irrelevant gates (e.g. docs-only repos skip T2 Feature Verification; repos without services skip T3 Integration Check)\\n- Enables custom shell-command gates analogous to no-mistakes `.no-mistakes/config.yaml` `command:` field\\n- Establishes a config-file convention (`.dh/quality-gates.yaml`) consistent with the existing `.dh/` project-config pattern\\n- Fallback to 6-phase default preserves backward compatibility for projects without the config file\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen `.dh/quality-gates.yaml` is present in the project root, `/complete-implementation` reads it and constructs the QG plan from only the gates declared in that file, in the declared order. When the file is absent, the full 6-phase default plan is used, identical to current behavior. A project with 3 gates declared in the file produces a 3-task QG plan; running `/complete-implementation` dispatches exactly those 3 tasks, no more.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\n- `.dh/quality-gates.yaml` in project root: per-project gate configuration (consumed by the plugin at runtime; not part of plugin source)\\n- `sam_schema/core/quality_gates.py`: `build_quality_gate_plan()` gains a `gates_config` parameter that is typed (a Pydantic model or TypedDict \u2014 never `dict[str, Any]`, never `cast`, never `object`) accepting the parsed config; when `None`, falls back to `_PHASE_DEFINITIONS`\\n- A typed Pydantic model for the gate config schema so schema violations are caught at parse time (not at plan-generation time)\\n- `complete-implementation/SKILL.md` dispatch loop: gains a config-read step before calling `build_quality_gate_plan()`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/references/gate-config-schema.md`: schema documentation as stated in item's measurable signal\\n- The T5 auto-skip logic in SKILL.md must either be generalised (applicable to any gate whose predecessor reports no relevant findings) or documented as a special case that applies only when T4 is present in its standard position\\n\\nDesign constraint (type safety): the config reader must not use `cast`, `Any`, or `object` as a substitute for proper modelling. The Pydantic model must improve typing in `quality_gates.py`, not weaken it. Running `uv run ty check plugins/development-harness/` must produce no new type errors after this change.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. Create `.dh/quality-gates.yaml` with 3 gates (omitting T2 and T3). Run `/complete-implementation #N`. The created QG plan contains exactly 3 task IDs and no others \u2014 verified by reading the SAM plan via `sam_plan(action='status')`.\\n2. Delete `.dh/quality-gates.yaml` (or leave it absent). Run `/complete-implementation #N`. The created QG plan contains exactly 6 task IDs (T1\u2013T6), identical to current behavior.\\n3. The config parser rejects an invalid config (e.g. unknown agent name, duplicate task ID) with a clear error \u2014 it does not silently fall back to defaults.\\n4. The gate config is parsed into a typed Pydantic model or TypedDict \u2014 not `dict[str, Any]` and not `cast`. Running `uv run ty check plugins/development-harness/` passes with no new type errors introduced by this change.\\n5. `gate-config-schema.md` exists at `plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/references/gate-config-schema.md` and documents all fields (`name`, `enabled`, `agent`, `command`, `auto_fix`) with types and defaults.\\n6. Existing tests for `build_quality_gate_plan()` still pass: `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/ -k quality_gate`.\\n\\n### Questions for Human\\n\\n- Should the proportional quality gates path (`build_proportional_quality_gate_plan`, used when an issue has no linked SAM plan) also be made configurable via the same file, or is that out of scope for this item?\\n- When a custom `command:` gate is declared (shell command instead of agent), how should it integrate with the SAM dispatch loop? The loop dispatches tasks to agents via `start-task` \u2014 a shell command gate cannot use that path. Should it run as a pre-check before the SAM loop, or as a synthetic task dispatched to `task-worker`?\\n- Should the T5 auto-skip (currently hardcoded to detect phase 4 drift) be generalised to work for any gate whose predecessor reports no relevant findings, or remain a special case?\\n- If a project config declares an `agent:` value that overrides the default agent for a phase, should the agent name be validated against the registered agent inventory at config-read time (see #1113)?\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Source file | `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/quality_gates.py` \u2014 `_PHASE_DEFINITIONS` (lines 24\u201373), `build_quality_gate_plan()` (lines 116\u2013171) |\\n| Source file | `plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md` \u2014 dispatch loop (lines 442\u2013513), T5 skip logic (lines 504\u2013506) |\\n| Source file | `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py` \u2014 `Task` and `Plan` Pydantic models (reference for typed gate config model design) |\\n| Research | `research/developer-tools/no-mistakes.md` \u2014 Multi-Stage Composable Gates pattern, `.no-mistakes/config.yaml` schema (gates array with name/enabled/command/auto_fix) |\\n| Related item | #1113 \u2014 Agent name reference audit (agent name validation at config-read time is relevant) |\\n| Related item | #1672 \u2014 doc-drift-auditor concept scope (affects T4 behavior, relevant to T5 skip generalisation) |\\n| Skill | /dh:complete-implementation \u2014 the skill being extended |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None (no blocking prerequisite)\\n- Blocks: None directly; #1113 (agent name audit) would complement the config validation step added here\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\n- Human answers needed on PQG path scope, custom command gate dispatch mechanism, and T5-skip generalisation before full implementation can begin (see Questions for Human)\\n- No blocking technical prerequisites\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nMedium \u2014 Core change is adding a typed Pydantic model for the gate config, a YAML reader in `build_quality_gate_plan()`, and a config-read step in the SKILL.md dispatch loop. Primary complexity is resolving the T5-skip interaction (generalise or special-case) and the custom command gate dispatch mechanism. Test surface: new config-parsing tests plus existing pure-function tests for `quality_gates.py`.\\n\\n## Source\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nResearch entry: ./research/developer-tools/no-mistakes.md \u2014 Multi-Stage Validation Gates pattern with YAML config example.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Current State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThe 6 quality-gate phases (T1\u2013T6) are hardcoded in `build_quality_gate_plan()` (referenced lines 411\u2013414 of `plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md`, defined in `sam_schema.core.quality_gates`). The phase-task mapping table (lines 446\u2013456) lists T1=Code Review, T2=Feature Verification, T3=Integration Check, T4=Documentation Drift Audit, T5=Documentation Update, T6=Context Refinement \u2014 fixed agents, fixed order, fixed dependency chain. There is no per-project config file analogous to no-mistakes' `.no-mistakes/config.yaml` `gates:` array where a project owner can disable phases (e.g., a docs-only repo might skip Feature Verification), reorder them, or substitute a custom shell-command gate (e.g., `command: ./scripts/check-license-headers.sh`). The only conditional skip is T5 when T4 reports no drift (lines 504\u2013506).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Target State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nA `.dh/quality-gates.yaml` file in the project root declares the active gate sequence: each entry has `name`, `enabled`, optional `agent` (defaults from build_quality_gate_plan), optional `command` (custom shell gate), and optional `auto_fix` flag. `build_quality_gate_plan()` reads this file when present and emits the SAM plan based on the declared sequence; falls back to the existing 6-phase default when no file exists. The Quality Gate Plan Creation section of complete-implementation/SKILL.md documents the config schema and the precedence (project config > default).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Measurable Signal\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nCreate `.dh/quality-gates.yaml` with 3 gates (e.g., omit T2 and T3). Run `/complete-implementation #N`. The created QG plan contains exactly those 3 task IDs, no more. Without the file, the plan still contains all 6 default tasks. Schema documented in `complete-implementation/SKILL.md` and in a new reference file `plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/references/gate-config-schema.md`.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"2797ca3c94539ba0bb7dcda29535c288bb05d57122094278edbf4e58eadeb01a\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPvc8ow\"}"}